2,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1998,3]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/(sici)1521-396x(199803)166:1<445::aid-pssa445>3.0.co;2-n","ISSN":["0031-8965","1521-396X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0031-8965","type":"print"},{"value":"1521-396X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1998,3]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,3]],"date-time":"2025-09-03T10:12:28Z","timestamp":1756894348869},"reference-count":16,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2006,2,7]],"date-time":"2006-02-07T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1139270400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":10690,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Physica Status Solidi (b)"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1976,11]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>The structure of the (100) and (110) surface of crystalline lithium hydride is calculated by the FSGO pair\u2010potential approximation. An outward displacement of the hydride ions and an inward displacement of the lithium ions relative to the ideal surface is determined in the case of the (100) surface. Also an alternating arrangement of the particles of the first and second surface layer is noticed. An inward displacement takes place not only for the lithium ions but also for the hydride ions in the case of the (110) surface. The surface energies and the ratio of the surface energies of the (110) and (100) surface are calculated in good agreement with semi\u2010empirical values of alkali halide crystals.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/pssb.2220780117","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,7,10]],"date-time":"2007-07-10T08:57:52Z","timestamp":1184057872000},"page":"183-189","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3,"title":["Quantum mechanical ab initio calculations of the surface structure of crystalline lithium hydride"],"prefix":"10.1002"